Keep the .rld_map section in IRIX5-compatible output

Upstream commit e6aea42dfaf13c0e0ca10fa604537a2f43ce9ae9 (Maciej W.
Rozycki, 2012-12-03, PR ld/10629) replaced the .rld_map creation arm
`IRIX_COMPAT (abfd) == ict_irix5 || IRIX_COMPAT (abfd) == ict_none` with
`!use_rld_obj_head`. IRIX crt1.o defines __rld_obj_head, so the o32
(ict_irix5) output no longer creates the section: DT_MIPS_RLD_MAP names a
slot in the .sbss tail and the guest o32 smoke dies at startup, where the
working 2.20.1 and SGUG 2.23.2 links carry the section and the map slot
inside the RW segment. Restore the ict_irix5 arm while keeping the modern
!use_rld_obj_head rule for every other MIPS target, and keep
DT_MIPS_RLD_MAP_REL (upstream a5499fa464, 2015).

Effect on the o32 hello signature: .rld_map reappears in the output and
the runtime linker's map slot is inside the RW segment tail as in the
2.20.1 baseline; see docs/binutils.md. Guest validation pending.

--- a/bfd/elfxx-mips.c
+++ b/bfd/elfxx-mips.c
@@ -8126,8 +8126,11 @@
     return false;
   htab->sstubs = s;
 
-  if (!mips_elf_hash_table (info)->use_rld_obj_head
-      && bfd_link_executable (info)
+  /* IRIX5-compatible output keeps the .rld_map marker even when crt1.o
+     supplies __rld_obj_head; upstream e6aea42dfa removed that arm.  */
+  if (bfd_link_executable (info)
+      && (IRIX_COMPAT (abfd) == ict_irix5
+	  || !mips_elf_hash_table (info)->use_rld_obj_head)
       && bfd_get_linker_section (abfd, ".rld_map") == NULL)
     {
       s = bfd_make_section_anyway_with_flags (abfd, ".rld_map",
